Here's a JavaScript function that accepts text and posts messages via the Slack API to the specified channel:

```javascript
function postToSlackChannel(text, channel) {
  const token = 'YOUR_SLACK_API_TOKEN'; // Replace with your Slack API token
  const url = `https://slack.com/api/chat.postMessage?token=${token}&channel=${channel}`;

  fetch(url, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      text: text
    })
  })
    .then(response => response.json())
    .then(data => console.log('Message posted to Slack:', data))
    .catch(error => console.error('Error posting to Slack:', error));
}

// Example usage
postToSlackChannel('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

Replace `'YOUR_SLACK_API_TOKEN'` with your actual Slack API token and `'#general'` with the channel you want to post the message to. You can call this function with any text you want to post and the channel you want to post it to.

