def find_max(array):
    max_value = array[0]
    for i in range(1, len(array)):
        if array[i] > max_value:
            max_value = array[i]
    return max_value
```

This algorithm works by initializing the `max_value` variable to the first element of the array. It then loops through the remaining elements of the array, comparing each one to the current `max_value`. If the current element is greater than the `max_value`, it updates the `max_value` variable to the current element. Finally, it returns the `max_value` variable.

