To pass credentials in JS code using `react-native-fbsdk-next`, you can follow these steps:

1. First, make sure you have installed the required packages:
```bash
npm install react-native-fbsdk-next
```
2. Next, create a new file named `Credentials.js` and add the following code:
```javascript
import { FacebookAuthProvider } from 'react-native-fbsdk';

const credentials = new FacebookAuthProvider({
  appId: 'YOUR_APP_ID',
  appName: 'YOUR_APP_NAME',
  apiVersion: 'YOUR_API_VERSION',
});

export default credentials;
```
Replace `YOUR_APP_ID`, `YOUR_APP_NAME`, and `YOUR_API_VERSION` with your actual Facebook app ID, app name, and API version.
3. Now, you can import the `credentials` object in your other JS files and use it to authenticate users with Facebook:
```javascript
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { View, Text, Button } from 'react-native';
import { credentials } from './Credentials';

const App = () => {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);

  const handleLogin = async () => {
    try {
      const result = await credentials.login();
      console.log('Logged in as:', result.user);
      setUser(result.user);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error logging in:', error);
    }
  };

  return (
    <View>
      <Text>Welcome!</Text>
      <Button title="Login with Facebook" onPress={handleLogin} />
      {user && <Text>Signed in as {user.name}</Text>}
    </View>
  );
};

export default App;
```
This example demonstrates how to pass credentials in JS code using `react-native-fbsdk-next`. You can customize the `credentials` object to suit your specific needs and integrate it into your existing React Native application.

